@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# draft-advisor-master-data: Read advisor master data from the ERP
+
+- **Jira:** none yet (a person must create or name the story; then move this folder to `docs/specs/AN-<n>/`)
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2: a new ERP port operation and payload contract; trigger 5: a synchronous ERP read outside T2 section 4 and T3-D-007, see [CR-001](../../changes/CR-001-synchronous-advisor-read.md))
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: integration (new public API `readAdvisor`, called by `identity`), erp-port (new operation), erp-fake (seed advisor), apps/worker (wiring)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs the advisor master data that the ERP holds (T2-C-010). The ERP is reached only through `integration` and its port (T3-D-005). ADR-0017 records the decision.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+The register has no AC ID for this request. The criteria of the request, without an ID until the story names one:
+
+| Criterion | Test |
+|---|---|
+| `identity.getAdvisor("B20001")` returns the seed advisor with `sourceVersion` and `readAt` | `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts`, `packages/core/src/integration/integration.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+| `getAdvisor` returns `null` when the ERP has no such advisor | same files |
+| `app.identity.getAdvisor` is wired in `createApp()` | `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+| The fake ERP seeds advisor `B20001` that satisfies `AdvisorMasterData` | `packages/erp-fake/src/erp-fake.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file (`identity`):** `createIdentity({ repo, bus, integration, clock })`; `.getAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<Advisor | null>`; type `Advisor = { advisorNumber, givenName, familyName, email, active, sourceVersion, readAt }`. Invariant: advisor master data is read on each call, not stored, and carries `sourceVersion` and `readAt` (ADR-0017).
+- **Module file (`integration`):** `Integration.readAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<ErpRead<AdvisorMasterData> | null>`.
+- **Contracts:** ERP port operation `readAdvisor(advisorNumber): Promise<AdvisorMasterData | null>`. Payload `AdvisorMasterData`: `advisorNumber` (`^B\d{5}$`), `givenName`, `familyName`, `email` (e-mail), `active` (boolean), `sourceVersion`. No events.
+- **Schema:** none. Nothing is stored.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- `identity` defines its own `Advisor` type instead of re-exporting the port type: other modules must not depend on `@provital/erp-port` (T3-D-005).
+- An ERP outage is not mapped to `null`: `ErpUnavailableError` reaches the caller, who decides the fallback ([ERP conventions](../../conventions/erp.md)).
+- Seed advisor `B20001` matches the advisor of seed customer `K100001`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- A stored copy of advisors, the customer–advisor assignment, roles of a person who is an advisor (T3-D-009).
+- A head office screen or endpoint that calls `getAdvisor`.
+- Authorisation of the caller.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Which AC ID, if any, covers this story? The register has none for advisor master data reads.
+- A synchronous ERP read, or a read copy behind the same API? See CR-001. The code implements the synchronous read that was asked for.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
